# Every text file checks out with LF line endings on every platform.
#
# The fleet CI floor (C4-tests-yml) runs the suite on Windows, whose hosted
# runners set core.autocrlf=true: without this file a checkout there rewrites
# every text file to CRLF, and anything that hashes a file's BYTES — the
# fleet conventions document's pin in tests/test_fleet_conventions.py, the
# bodies tools/vendor_sync_check.py reads when it is asked for bytes rather
# than text — stops matching the number recorded on Linux. Pinning the
# checkout to LF is the fix at the source; normalising CRLF away in each
# reader would only hide which platform the bytes came from.
* text=auto eol=lf
